# L §6.4 "A scenario row may be an expression over the base's facts, the base's items named with the base's id as a
# prefix and the scenario's own items bare (replace sale_price[flat] = household.valuation[flat] * keep_share, with
# keep_share a scenario input) ... The expression is evaluated at the row's keys and law date: its prefixed names in
# the base, its bare names in the scenario."
# Base: valuation[flat] 800 000.00 PLN, sale_price[flat] 700 000.00 PLN, bare_price[flat] 650 000.00 PLN.  Scenario
# sell (from 2031-01-01) replaces valuation[flat] with 1 000 000.00 PLN, keep_share = 0.9, and from 2031 gives
# sale_price = household.valuation * keep_share and bare_price = valuation * keep_share.
# a1 (in sell, law 2031-06-30): sale_price reads the base's valuation: 800 000 * 0.9 = 720 000.00 PLN; bare_price
# reads the scenario's: 1 000 000 * 0.9 = 900 000.00 PLN.  a2: the base is unchanged (700 000.00, 650 000.00 PLN).
# a3: before the scenario's rows govern (law 2030-06-30), the base's rows: 700 000.00 PLN.
# a4: loop = loop * keep_share reads itself in the scenario, at the same key: RUN-CYCLE (L §8.4 table, `<x>[k]
# reads itself through <path>`).
# The linked figures are num PLN, as L §6.4 now declares sale_price ("with sale_price a num PLN input of the base",
# round 8): a money times a num is a num CUR (L §3.2).
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2040-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index flats = [flat]
input valuation[f in flats]: money PLN
input sale_price[f in flats]: num PLN
input bare_price[f in flats]: num PLN
input loop: num PLN

version base_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  valuation[flat] = 800 000.00 PLN "operat"
  sale_price[flat] = 700 000.00 PLN "oferta"
  bare_price[flat] = 650 000.00 PLN "oferta"
  loop = 1.00 PLN "own"

ask a2: sale_price[flat], bare_price[flat] law 2031-06-30
=== sell.tally
scenario sell over household
  tally 2
  from 2031-01-01

input keep_share: num

version sell_2031
  cite plan
  governs 2031-01-01..
  known 2026-10-20
  replace valuation[flat] = 1 000 000.00 PLN "założenie"
  keep_share = 0.9 "założenie"
  replace sale_price[flat] = household.valuation[flat] * keep_share "powiązana cena"
  replace bare_price[flat] = valuation[flat] * keep_share "powiązana cena"
  replace loop = loop * keep_share "pętla"

ask a1: sale_price[flat], bare_price[flat] in sell law 2031-06-30
ask a3: sale_price[flat] in sell law 2030-06-30
ask a4: loop in sell law 2031-06-30
=== expect
a1: (720 000 PLN, 900 000 PLN)
  world: sell
...
a2: (700 000 PLN, 650 000 PLN)
...
a3: 700 000 PLN
  world: sell
...
a4: refused: RUN-CYCLE ...
...
